# The /app Vite sandbox is a dev-only component studio -- its entry points at
# /src/main.jsx, which only resolves under the dev server. On the deployed
# site it renders a blank page and hands out raw .jsx sources, so keep it off
# the production domain. Run it locally with `npm run dev` instead.
# The ! is required: Netlify serves a matching static file in preference to
# a redirect rule unless the status is forced, and app/index.html is real.
/app/*    /404.html    404!

# Canonical URLs are extensionless (see the rel=canonical in every page head).
# Netlify already *serves* /electro-installation for electro-installation.html,
# so without these rules both spellings return 200 and Google files the clean
# one as a duplicate. These make the .html spelling a 301 to the canonical one.
# The ! is required for the same reason as the rule above: the .html file is
# real, and Netlify prefers a matching static file over an unforced redirect.
#
# thanks.html is deliberately absent: it is the Netlify form POST target
# (action="/thanks.html") and is noindex, so it needs no clean URL and
# redirecting it would add a hop to every form submission.
/index.html                       /                             301!
/terraces.html                    /terraces                     301!
/electro-installation.html        /electro-installation         301!
/gothic-modern-architecture.html  /gothic-modern-architecture   301!
/classical-precision.html         /classical-precision          301!
/architects.html                  /architects                   301!
/privacy.html                     /privacy                      301!
/en/index.html                    /en/                          301!
/en/terraces.html                 /en/terraces                  301!
/en/electro-installation.html     /en/electro-installation      301!
/en/gothic-modern-architecture.html /en/gothic-modern-architecture 301!
/en/classical-precision.html      /en/classical-precision       301!
/en/architects.html               /en/architects                301!
/en/privacy.html                  /en/privacy                   301!
